                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A very well done detective game. The story of a famous writer who was murdered in a cabin. In the same time, detective Alicia was visiting that town for her vacation which seems to be cut short due to the sheriff's request for her help. Accepting his request, Alicia starts her investigation. I enjoyed the story which contains four chapters, once you finish a chapter, the investigation will move to another area which will not allow you to re-visit the previous locations even with the fast traveling map which the game has. \n\nThis game doesn't have any hidden objects scenes, however, it has many puzzles which varies from easy to hard. I loved the game's art, loved everything about the details and colors choice. The characters design wasn't bad, but not the best. \nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1347270600\nhttp://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1347422142\n\nThey did a very good job with the voice overs especially the main character. It is rare to hear the character commenting on everything happens and doesn't sound like a loop. I found her sarcastic comments funny. \n\nI liked the addition of the very good and useful journal which keeps track of the story, characters bio and your gaming experience (How many puzzles you've skipped/solved and how many hints you've used!)\n\nPros:\n+Beautiful graphics.\n+Good soundtracks.\n+Interesting detective story.\n+Good voice overs.\n+Fast travel map.\n+Steam achievements.\n\nCons:\n-The cutscenes seem a little bit slow.\n\nJudging from the ending, the game seems to promise a sequel which I can't wait for! I do recommend this game for casual adventure gamers who love puzzles!\n\n[quote]𝐹𝑜𝑟 𝑚𝑜𝑟𝑒 𝑟𝑒𝑣𝑖𝑒𝑤𝑠 𝑐𝘩𝑒𝑐𝑘 𝑚𝑦 𝑐𝑢𝑟𝑎𝑡𝑜𝑟 𝑝𝑎𝑔𝑒 [url=http://store.steampowered.com/curator/32399565/]𝐹𝑒𝑒𝑛𝑎'𝑠 𝐶𝘩𝑜𝑖𝑐𝑒[/url][/quote]",
